%I A399107 #26 Sep 09 2026 10:57:59
%S A399107 1,1,2,5,19,102,730,6857,83654,1315378,26554439,686663981,22710272445,
%T A399107 959632731065
%N A399107 Number of nonisomorphic posets on n elements with trivial automorphism group.
%C A399107 A poset is counted if its automorphism group is trivial. Equivalently, these are rigid (asymmetric) unlabeled posets.
%C A399107 The terms were computed by recursively extending nonisomorphic posets: a new maximal element is adjoined over order ideals, with ideals reduced to orbits under the automorphism group of the parent poset. The resulting posets are tested for trivial automorphism group, with correction for the number of maximal elements. The value a(8) was also independently verified using Mobius inversion over the conjugacy classes of subgroups of S_8 and the Table of Marks of S_8.
%C A399107 G. Pfeiffer's data classify posets by conjugacy class of the automorphism group for n <= 12. Aggregating by group order agrees, for every n <= 12 and every order, with B. D. McKay's independent table. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 07 2026
%H A399107 Gunnar Brinkmann and Brendan D. McKay, <a href="https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/papers/posets.pdf">Posets on up to 16 Points</a>, Order 19 (2002), 147-179.
%H A399107 Götz Pfeiffer, <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL7/Pfeiffer/pfeiffer6.html">Counting Transitive Relations</a>, J. Int. Seq. 7 (2004), Art. 04.3.2.
%F A399107 a(n) = T_E(S_n)/n!, where T_E(S_n) is the number of labeled posets on n elements whose automorphism group is trivial.
%F A399107 a(n) = T_E(S_n)/n!, where T_E(S_n) = Sum_{[H] <= S_n} |S_n:N_{S_n}(H)|*mu(H)*F_n(H). Here the sum is over the conjugacy classes of subgroups H of S_n, mu(H) is the subgroup-lattice Mobius function, N_{S_n}(H) is the normalizer of H in S_n, and F_n(H) is the number of labeled posets on {1,...,n} fixed by H.
%e A399107 For n = 5, the 19 rigid posets may be represented by the following sets of covering relations on {1,2,3,4,5}; (i,j) means that i is covered by j:
%e A399107 {(1,2),(1,3),(4,2)}; {(1,2),(1,4),(2,3)}; {(1,2),(2,3),(3,4)}; {(1,2),(2,3),(4,3)}; {(1,2),(2,3),(4,5)}; {(1,2),(1,4),(2,3),(5,2)}; {(1,2),(1,4),(2,3),(5,3)}; {(1,2),(1,4),(2,3),(5,4)}; {(1,2),(1,5),(2,3),(3,4)}; {(1,2),(2,3),(2,4),(5,3)}; {(1,2),(2,3),(2,5),(3,4)}; {(1,2),(2,3),(3,4),(4,5)}; {(1,2),(2,3),(3,4),(5,3)}; {(1,2),(2,3),(3,4),(5,4)}; {(1,2),(2,3),(4,3),(4,5)}; {(1,2),(1,4),(2,3),(4,3),(5,2)}; {(1,2),(1,4),(2,3),(5,3),(5,4)}; {(1,2),(1,5),(2,3),(2,4),(5,3)}; {(1,2),(1,5),(2,3),(3,4),(5,4)}.
%Y A399107 Cf. A000112 (number of nonisomorphic posets on n elements); A091070 (number of distinct automorphism groups of posets with n elements).
